      "id": "kpk1-l15-b4-t01",
      "before": "kpk1-l15-b4-e01",
      "title": {
        "en": "Kotów, książek, jabłek"
      },
      "body": {
        "en": "In the genitive plural most masculine nouns that end in a hard sound take *-ów* (*kot*, *kotów*; *owoc*, *owoców*), and most feminine nouns in *-a* and neuter nouns in *-o* lose their ending, often with an *-e-* put in (*książka*, *książek*; *jabłko*, *jabłek*; *koleżanka*, *koleżanek*). Many nouns ending in *-l* take *-i*: *nauczyciel*, *nauczycieli*; *serial*, *seriali*. There are other endings too, met word by word. An adjective takes *-ych*: *nowych książek*, *fajnych koleżanek*; after *k* or *g* it is *-ich*: *polskich*."
      }
    }
  ],
